## How to Play topics (guide/guide-pages.ts). %1$s is a line break.
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.welcome=Welcome
wm_kitchen.guide.text.welcome=Simmerfield adds six new crops and a kitchen to cook them in. Grow the crops, cut them, mix them and cook them into dishes.%1$s%1$sEvery dish fills you up, and most also give you a helpful effect.
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.loop=The kitchen loop
wm_kitchen.guide.text.loop=1. Break grass for seeds%1$s2. Grow the crops%1$s3. Cut them on a Cutting Board%1$s4. Craft a mix on a crafting table%1$s5. Cook it in a Cooking Pot over a fire%1$s6. Eat!
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.seeds=Finding seeds
wm_kitchen.guide.text.seeds=Break grass or ferns and you will sometimes find a seed. Each crop likes certain places (see Crops), but every seed can turn up anywhere, just less often.%1$s%1$sShears and Creative mode find none.
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.farmland=Growing crops
wm_kitchen.guide.text.farmland=Plant tomato, cucumber and eggplant seeds on farmland, like wheat. An onion has no seeds: plant the onion itself.%1$s%1$sBreak a fully grown crop to get the crop and seeds back. Bone meal helps it grow.
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.bushes=Bushes
wm_kitchen.guide.text.bushes=Chili peppers and strawberries grow on bushes. Plant their seeds on grass, dirt or farmland.%1$s%1$sWhen a bush is ripe, use it to pick the fruit. The bush stays and grows more.
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.board=Cutting Board
wm_kitchen.guide.text.board=Craft it from a stick and two planks in a row.%1$s%1$sHold a tomato, onion, cucumber or eggplant and use the board to cut it. Sneak and use to cut the whole stack.
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.mixes=Mixes
wm_kitchen.guide.text.mixes=Hot dishes start as a mix. Craft the raw ingredients, usually with a bowl, on a crafting table.%1$s%1$sThe crafting table's recipe book shows every mix you have unlocked.
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.pot=Cooking Pot
wm_kitchen.guide.text.pot=Craft it from five iron ingots and a bowl. It only cooks with heat below: a campfire, fire, lava, a magma block or a lit Kitchen Stove.%1$s%1$sUse the pot with a mix in your hand to put it in. Sneak to add the whole stack.
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.cooking=Cooking
wm_kitchen.guide.text.cooking=The pot holds four mixes and cooks every mix of one dish at once.%1$s%1$sUse it with an empty hand to start cooking. When it's done, use it with an empty hand again to take your dishes.
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.cold=Cold dishes
wm_kitchen.guide.text.cold=Salads, salsa, sandwiches, the skewer and the strawberry treats need no pot: craft them on a crafting table.%1$s%1$sPlace a Strawberry Cake and use it to eat a slice.
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.effects=Effects
wm_kitchen.guide.text.effects=Most dishes give an effect for a while. Its color tells you what kind:%1$s%1$s§c❤ Red§r heals you%1$s§9▶ Blue§r moves you%1$s§e■ Yellow§r speeds up digging%1$s§a● Green§r helps you explore
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.poster=Recipe Poster
wm_kitchen.guide.text.poster=Craft it from paper and any Simmerfield crop, then hang it on a wall 2 blocks wide.%1$s%1$sUse it to see the dish and its effect. Sneak and use to turn to the next recipe.
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.unlocking=Unlocking recipes
wm_kitchen.guide.text.unlocking=Each new crop you find unlocks the recipes that use it: in this guide, on your Recipe Poster and in the crafting table's recipe book. Until then they show as ???.%1$s%1$sIn Creative mode everything is unlocked.
wm_kitchen.guide.topic.lost=Lost this book?
wm_kitchen.guide.text.lost=Craft a new one from a book and a carrot. It fits the small crafting grid in your inventory.%1$s%1$sHappy cooking!

